            <ArticleTitle>[Metabolic risk factors in heart surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Accelerated coronary atherosclerosis is a common complication following coronary angioplasty, coronary venous bypass grafting, and heart transplantation. Since dyslipoproteinemias are a major risk for atherosclerotic lesions, a consequent and effective lipid-regulating treatment is mandatory in these patients. The CLAS-findings are an impressive documentation for the beneficial effects of a substantial lipid-regulating treatment on progression and even repression of atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
